        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "afee0fd0-6c9a-53c3-b24c-b5dd3c0f36aa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: Project Sabre II\n- Products: Chengdu J-7, PAC JF-17 Thunder, CAC FC-1 Xiaolong, Chengdu F-7 Skybolt, MiG-21FL\n- Organizations: Pakistan Aeronautical Complex, Chengdu Aircraft Corporation, Pakistan Air Force\n\nFacts:\n- Project Sabre II was a Pakistan Air Force program to develop a feasible, low-cost multirole combat jet based on the Chengdu F-7 Skybolt, which was a Chinese variant of the MiG-21FL.\n- The Chengdu J-7 was extensively redeveloped into the CAC/PAC JF-17 Thunder, which became a successor to the J-7.\n- The PAC JF-17 Thunder, also called the CAC FC-1 Xiaolong, is a lightweight, single-engine, multirole combat aircraft.\n- The PAC JF-17 Thunder was developed jointly by the Pakistan Aeronautical Complex and the Chengdu Aircraft Corporation of China.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
